From: Woohyeon Baek
Subject: [PATCH] allocator_support: keep the thread-local cache lookup out of line

A function that suspends and resumes on another worker must not reach the
thread-local cache through a thread-local base computed before the
suspension; an out-of-line accessor recomputes it on each call.
---
--- a/libs/core/allocator_support/include/hpx/allocator_support/thread_local_caching_allocator.hpp
+++ b/libs/core/allocator_support/include/hpx/allocator_support/thread_local_caching_allocator.hpp
@@ -119,7 +119,13 @@
             std::size_t deallocated = 0;
         };
 
-        allocated_cache& cache()
+        // An HPX thread can suspend inside a caller and resume on a different
+        // worker. Kept out of line, the thread-local object is looked up on
+        // every call against the worker that is running now; inlined, a
+        // compiler may reuse a thread-local base it computed before the
+        // suspension, and the cache (and the destructor registered for it)
+        // would belong to the previous worker.
+        HPX_NOINLINE allocated_cache& cache()
         {
             thread_local allocated_cache allocated_data(alloc);
             return allocated_data;
